# format:
# - case inensitive
# - title line: "TITLE <tone-seq-name> <initial-octave>
# - tone sequence items:
#     C D E F G A B         : pitches in scientific pitch notation (SPN), in current octave
#     Cn Dn En Fn Gn An Bn  : pitches in SPN, where 'n' is the octave number, e.g. C4
#     do re mi fa sol la ti : solfege syllables, do=C re=D, ...
#     <n> up down           : set octave to 'n', or increase, or decrease octave
#     pause1 pause2 pause4  : delay for 250, 500, 1000 ms
# - an implicit pause2 is appended to the end of each line of items

TITLE ttls 5  # Twinkle Twinkle Little Star
C C G G A A G
F F E E D D C
G G F F E E D
G G F F E E D
C C G G A A G
F F E E D D C

TITLE mary 5  # Mary Had a Little Lamb
E D C D E E E
D D D
E G G
E D C D E E E E D D E D C 

TITLE fj 5  # Frere Jacques
C D E C pause1 C D E C
E F G pause1 E F G
G A G F E C pause1 G A G F E C
C G C pause1 C G C

TITLE jbells 5  # Jingle Bells
E E E pause1 E E E
E G C D E
F F F F F E E
E D D E D pause1 G
E E E pause1 E E E
E G C D E
F F F F F E E
G G F D C

TITLE ag 5  # Amazing Grace
C E G E G E D C      # A-ma-zing grace! How sweet the sound
C E G E G A C        # That saved a wretch like me!
C C A G E G E D C    # I once was lost, but now am found
C E G E G A C        # Was blind, but now I see.

TITLE doremi3 3  # Natural notes in octave 3
C D E F G A B

TITLE doremi4 4  # Natural notes in octave 4
C D E F G A B

TITLE doremi5 5  # Natural notes in octave 5
do re mi fa sol la ti

TITLE doremi6 6  # Natural notes in octave 6
C D E F G A B
